        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.sources.source_addresses` has two behavioral obligations. The reviewed tests cover both.\n\n**1. Source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values.**\n- `gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository` checks that `list` returns relative paths such as `keep.txt` and `src/nested.txt`. Its `read`, `parse` and `search_text` calls take relative file paths. It also asserts that `search_text` match paths equal `Path::new(\"src/nested.txt\")`.\n- `scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors` asserts that `listed[0]` equals `Path::new(\"src/one.txt\")`. That is a nested, project-relative path.\n- `empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct` checks that `parsed.id().path` is `note.txt`. It reads by a `PathBuf` and rejects `../` paths and absolute paths, so only project-relative addresses are accepted.\n- `built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope` asserts `found.matches[0].node.path == Path::new(\"visible.rs\")`. It makes the same check for `script.py`.\n- `local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root` covers the local provider's root-scoped resource locations and rejects outside resources.\n\n**2. An item within a file uses the `OutlineData` path and selector.**\n- `empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct` asserts that the file-level id has path `note.txt` and selector `\"\"`.\n- `built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope` asserts that the structural match node has path `visible.rs` and selector `fn[visible]`.\n- `outline_addresses_validate_selectors_without_reading_paths` and `addresses_preserve_opaque_fields_and_compare_each_identity_component` check path and selector preservation. The second also checks identity comparison on each field.\n\nThe identity and selector-validation rules belong to the cited `requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`, which is context only. I did not reassess its tests.\n\nI found no gap. All the reviewed tests already carry `{test}` markers for the subject."
      }
